          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            in (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"}> global
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %p
            Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-grading"} RO(G)-graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            are the equivariant version of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectrum"} equivariant suspension spectrum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo *
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0 = \ast_+
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{S} = \Sigma^\infty_G S^0
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0
            regarded as equipped with the (necessarily) trivial
            = succeed "-action." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            an orthogonal linear
            = succeed "-representation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-degree"} RO(G)-degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            the equivariant sphere spectrum is the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+sphere"} representation sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}(V) \simeq S^V
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwede15"} Schwede 15, example 2.10
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#EquivariantHomotopyGroups Equivariant homotopy groups
          %p
            Just as for the plain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+groups"} equivariant homotopy groups
            of the equivariant sphere spectrum in ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            are all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mi for
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi n
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mi otherwise
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_n^H(\mathbb{S})\otimes \mathbb{Q} =
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\cdots &amp; for \; n = 0
                  \\\
                  0 &amp; otherwise
                  }
                  \\right.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#GreenleesMay95"}> Greenlees-May 95, prop. A.3
            )
          %p
            But in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-degrees"} RO(G)-degrees
            there may appear further non-torsion groups, see the
            %a{:href => "#Examples"} examples
            below.
          %p
            In degree 0, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tom+Dieck+splitting"} tom Dieck splitting
            applied to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectrum"} equivariant suspension spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S} = \Sigma^\infty_G S^0
            gives that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0^G(\mathbb{S})
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
            on the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          #eq:pi_0ofEquivariantSphere.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi G
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi G
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi conjugacy
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi classes
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi of
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi subgroups
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0^G(\mathbb{S})
                  \\simeq
                  \\underset{[H \subset G]}{\oplus} \pi_0^{W_G H}(\Sigma_+^\infty E (W_G H))
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbb{Z}[conjugacy\;classes\;of\;subgroups]
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwede15"} Schwede 15, p. 64
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#Z2equivariance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            \-equivariance
          %p
            Consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G= \mathbb{Z}_2
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"} cyclic group of order 2
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{p,q}
            for the homotopy group in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RO%28G%29-grading"} RO(G)-degree
            given by the representation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p+q}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            acts by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflection"} reflection
            on the first
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            coordinates, and trivially on the remaining
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            coordinates:
          %p
            The following groups contain
            = succeed "-summands:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{0,0} = \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}
                (by the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Hopf+degree+theorem"} equivariant Hopf degree theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "Hopf+degree+theorem#EquivariantCohomotopyOfRepresentationSphereOfSignRepresentationInThatDegree"} this Example
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{1,0}
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 8.7, p. 25
                ) generated by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Hopf+fibration"} complex Hopf fibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \eta
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, p. 24
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{2,0}
                generated by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \eta^2
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 9.6, p. 27
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 3
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{3,0}
                generated by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \eta^3
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 10.11, p. 31
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{4,0}
                generated by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi η
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \eta^4
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 11.3, p. 32
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 5
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{5,0}
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 12.4, p. 34
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{6,0}
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 13.12, p. 38
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 7
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{7,0}
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 14.18, p. 45
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mn 8
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{8,0}
                (
                %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, theorem 15.26, p. 54
                )
          %p In addition we have
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                      %mi S
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 24
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^S_{2,1} \simeq \mathbb{Z}/24
              generated by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \nu
              (
              %a{:href => "#ArakiIriye82"}> Araki-Iriye 82, prop. 10.1, p. 28 with theorem 10.11, p. 31
              )
          %p#ArakiIriyeResultsTable
            In summary and more generally we have the following
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ArakiIriyeResults.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              The table shows the
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
